{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he called to it.</b> Like 'they said to me, my brother,' which is like עלי; the meaning is: and he called upon the altar, 'El, the Elohim of Israel,' and prayed to Him — and so is the translation of Onkelos. Here Rashi explained: not that the altar was called by the whole world 'Elohim of Israel,' but because HaShem was with him, Jacob alone called the name of the altar 'El, Elohei of Israel,' on account of the miracle — as we find nearby, 'and he called the place El Bethel,' and in Judges, 'and Gideon built there an altar and called it HaShem Shalom'; and so I explained in the perasha of Beshalach."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:16.889433151Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}